    <!-- Open signed centerline with a start and an end. World frame X north, Y east, Z down. A right turn has positive curvature. Built by tools/tracks/open_course.py from sections of linearly varying curvature. -->
    <!-- Source: Formula SAE Rules 2026, Version 1.0, 10 Sept 2025, https://www.fsaeonline.com/cdsweb/gen/DownloadDocument.aspx?DocumentID=278fd4d7-aa27-4e33-bc4a-090148e662a0 (PDF sha256 4620c33700f16bdc514a1e959b8746caef0a8878646c9b79b2ed01e8f790f7d8, fetched 2026-10-19). A later rules issue may differ. -->
    <!-- Generated by tools/tracks/build_fsae_dynamic_tracks.py. The point-mass solver reads the radius magnitude and the planar models read the signed curvature. -->
    <!-- D.10.1.1 centers 18.25 m apart, inner circles 15.25 m and outer circles 21.25 m in diameter, 3.0 m driving path. The path is the ring centerline, radius (15.25 + 21.25) / 4 = 9.125 m. D.10.2.3 the run is right lap (untimed), right lap (timed), left lap (untimed), left lap (timed), then exit. D.10.4.1 the scored time is the mean of the two timed laps. -->
    <!-- The entry and exit straights are modelling choices, not rule values, because the rules give the lane geometry only in a diagram. The course heads north from the origin and the circles touch at the end of the entry straight. Each curvature jump there is a 0.05 m ramp in the table. -->
    <!-- Curvature jumps, not smoothed: +0.109589 1/m at 15.0000 m; -0.219178 1/m at 129.7181 m; +0.109589 1/m at 244.4363 m. -->
